{"name":"Evening Glow","hex":"#fdd792","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"evening","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time of day between afternoon and night.","The time of the day between the approximate time of midwinter dusk and midnight (compare afternoon); the period after the end of regular office working hours."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of even"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evening"},{"term":"glow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To emit heat and light without a flame.","To emit heat and light without a flame."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of heat and light being emitted by a hot object.","A state of heat being emitted by a person or an animal's body."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evening","blocks":[{"text":"Evening is the period of a day that begins at the end of afternoon and overlaps with the beginning of night. It starts when the sun is close to the horizon and, according to most definitions, spans the period of night before bedtime or midnight. The exact times when evening begins and ends are subjective and depend on location and time of year. In some cases, evening is considered to begin during daylight; before sunset."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Evening_in_Parambikkulam%2C_Kerala%2C_India.jpg/330px-Evening_in_Parambikkulam%2C_Kerala%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evening"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Evening_view_on_the_bay_of_Naples%2C_overlooking_Mount_Vesuvius.jpg/500px-Evening_view_on_the_bay_of_Naples%2C_overlooking_Mount_Vesuvius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Evening_view_on_the_bay_of_Naples%2C_ov